<header>\
    <h1>CIPD Executive Coaching Guide</h1>\
</header>\
\
<div class="container">\
    <div class="intro-text">\
        Executive coaching has evolved from an informal "sounding board" into strategic tool of leadership development. Rigorous research confirms that EC significantly boosts mental resilience and professional agility. However, effective planning requires navigating the "perception gap" between a leader's enthusiasm for the process and their actual objective performance.\
    </div>\
\
    <section class="pillar-grid">\
        <div class="pillar-content">\
            <h2>1. Defining the Scope</h2>\
            <p>Executive Coaching (EC) is often conflated with mentoring or consulting. To ensure efficacy, it must be defined as a formal, three-way partnership between the coach, executive, and organisation. Distinguishing EC from remedial support is vital, as the quality of this partnership is the strongest predictor of success.</p>\
        </div>\
