                <rect x="20" y="55" width="25" height="25" rx="2" fill="var(--navy)" opacity="0.3"/>\
                <rect x="55" y="55" width="25" height="25" rx="2" fill="var(--teal)"/>\
                <path d="M50 10 V 90 M 10 50 H 90" stroke="var(--white)" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.5"/>\
            </svg>\
        </div>\
    </section>\
\
    <section class="pillar-grid">\
        <div class="pillar-content">\
            <h2>3. Readiness and Investment Risks</h2>\
            <p>Leaders most in need of development often resist the process. Beyond simple willingness, organisations should screen for an executive\'92s readiness to change. The ability to manage emotions and reactions is a critical foundation; pre-coaching assessments help avoid investing in leaders who are resistant to self-reflection.</p>\
        </div>\
        <div class="infographic-container">\
            <svg width="140" height="140" viewBox="0 0 100 100">\
                <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="none" stroke="var(--navy)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2 4"/>\
                <path d="M20 50 L40 50 L45 30 L55 70 L60 50 L80 50" fill="none" stroke="var(--teal)" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>\
            </svg>\
        </div>\
    </section>\
\
    <section class="pillar-grid">\
        <div class="pillar-content">\
            <h2>4. Evaluating Success</h2>\
            <p>The industry lacks standardised measurements, and relying solely on executive feedback forms can lead to biased results. Progress should be triangulated using feedback from others to provide objective ratings. Rather than focusing on simple financial ROI, success should be measured by how well the intervention fulfills specific strategic requirements.</p>\
        </div>\
        <div class="infographic-container">\
            <svg width="140" height="140" viewBox="0 0 100 100">\
                <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="10" fill="var(--teal)"/>\
